Front-side write tracking for the GPU thread split, part 1: a bitmap of device pages the emulated
GPU may have written. Ideas from Lichii PR #179 (https://github.com/zortos293/Lichii/pull/179:
the GPU-written page bitmap and the "new pages marked" counter behind EDEN_NX2_LIST_FAST) and #243
(https://github.com/zortos293/Lichii/pull/243: noting on the front which memory queued work can
write). Written for this core, not copied. The back marks a 4 KiB page when the buffer cache or the
texture cache records a GPU write there, when a query or semaphore result is queued for it
(RasterizerVulkan::Query), and when an engine writes guest memory through the memory manager.
Marks are never cleared. Only 99zzzt2 reads them; with the split off this costs one relaxed load
per mark.
